# React Flow Canvas — Main Canvas Page

Build a visual ontology modelling canvas on the "Main Canvas" (`/`) route using React Flow. The interface follows the same 3-pane layout as ArchiFlow: **left element palette → center canvas → right property panel**, but adapted for Knowledge Graph / RDF ontology modelling.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> This is a large feature. I recommend we build it **incrementally in phases** so you can test each piece before moving on. The plan below covers **Phase 1 (MVP)** which gives you a working canvas with shapes, drag-drop, property editing, and TTL import/export.

> [!WARNING]
> **Shapes for Ontology Modelling**: In ArchiFlow the shapes represent WAM components (service, application, etc). For KG Portal, what ontology shapes do you want? I'm proposing these defaults — please confirm or adjust:
> - **Class** (rounded rectangle) — `owl:Class`
> - **Object Property** (diamond) — `owl:ObjectProperty`
> - **Data Property** (hexagon) — `owl:DatatypeProperty`
> - **Instance** (circle) — `owl:NamedIndividual`
> - **Literal** (small rounded pill) — `rdfs:Literal`
> - **Connections**: `rdfs:subClassOf`, `rdfs:domain`, `rdfs:range`, `rdf:type` (as edge types)

---

## Phase 1 — MVP Proposed Changes

### Dependencies

Install `reactflow` (v11) into the frontend:
```
npm install reactflow
```

---

### Frontend — New Files

#### [NEW] `Canvas/CanvasEditor.jsx`
The **3-pane shell** layout component (mirrors ArchiFlow's [EditorLayout.tsx](file:///D:/Masters/2Y1S/Project%20-%2030sp/ArchiFlow-New/frontend/src/components/Canvas/EditorLayout.tsx)):
- State: `selectedItem`, `model` (nodes + edges), left/right panel collapse toggles
- Left: `<OntologyPalette />`
- Center: `<OntologyCanvas />` (React Flow)
- Right: `<PropertyPanel />`

#### [NEW] `Canvas/OntologyCanvas.jsx`
The **center React Flow canvas** (mirrors [MainCanvas.tsx](file:///D:/Masters/2Y1S/Project%20-%2030sp/ArchiFlow-New/frontend/src/components/Canvas/MainCanvas.tsx) but simplified for RDF):
- `ReactFlowProvider` wrapper with `useNodesState` + `useEdgesState`
- Drag-and-drop from palette via `onDrop` / `onDragOver`
- Custom node types for each shape (Class, Property, Instance, Literal)
- Edge connection logic with labelled relationship types
- MiniMap, Background grid, and Controls
- Toolbar row: Undo, Redo, Delete, Zoom controls

#### [NEW] `Canvas/OntologyPalette.jsx`
The **left-hand element palette** (mirrors [WamPalette.tsx](file:///D:/Masters/2Y1S/Project%20-%2030sp/ArchiFlow-New/frontend/src/components/Palette/WamPalette.tsx)):
- Collapsible accordion sections: "Classes", "Properties", "Instances"
- Each item is `draggable`, sets `dataTransfer` with the shape type
- Clean SVG icons for each shape type

#### [NEW] `Canvas/PropertyPanel.jsx`
The **right-hand property management panel** (mirrors [PropertyMngPanel.tsx](file:///D:/Masters/2Y1S/Project%20-%2030sp/ArchiFlow-New/frontend/src/components/Palette/PropertyMngPanel.tsx)):
- Two tabs: **Element** and **Import / Export**
- **Element Tab**: When a node/edge is selected, show editable fields:
  - Label, IRI (auto-generated or manual), Description
  - For edges: source handle, target handle, relationship type dropdown
- **Import/Export Tab**:
  - **Import**: File picker for `.ttl` / `.rdf` files → parse with backend `rdflib` and populate canvas
  - **Export**: Button to serialize current canvas model to Turtle (`.ttl`) and trigger download

#### [NEW] `Canvas/shapes/` (directory)
Custom React Flow node components:
- `ClassNode.jsx` — rounded rectangle with label
- `PropertyNode.jsx` — diamond shape with label
- `InstanceNode.jsx` — circle with label
- `LiteralNode.jsx` — small pill shape

#### [NEW] `Canvas/CanvasEditor.css`
- 3-pane flexbox layout (left 240px | center flex-1 | right 280px)
- Collapsible panel animations
- Palette item styling with drag cursor

---

### Frontend — Modified Files

#### [MODIFY] [App.jsx](file:///d:/Masters/KG_Portal/Knowledge_graph_portal/frontend/src/App.jsx)
- Import `CanvasEditor` and replace `<Home />` on the `/` route with `<CanvasEditor />`
- Keep Home as a separate route if needed (e.g. `/home`)

---

### Backend — RDF Parsing Endpoint

#### [MODIFY] [router.py](file:///d:/Masters/KG_Portal/Knowledge_graph_portal/backend/routers/router.py) + [controller.py](file:///d:/Masters/KG_Portal/Knowledge_graph_portal/backend/controllers/controller.py)
- Add `POST /canvas/import` — accepts a TTL file upload, parses it with `rdflib`, and returns a JSON structure of `{ nodes: [...], edges: [...] }` so the frontend can populate the canvas.
- Add `POST /canvas/export` — accepts the canvas JSON model and returns serialized Turtle content as a downloadable response.

---

## Verification Plan

### Manual Testing
1. Open `/` — verify the 3-pane layout renders with palette, empty canvas, and property panel
2. Drag a "Class" shape from palette → drops onto canvas as a rounded rectangle node
3. Click the node → right panel shows editable label, IRI, description fields
4. Connect two nodes → edge appears with a relationship label
5. Export → downloads a `.ttl` file with valid RDF triples
6. Import a `.ttl` file → canvas populates with nodes and edges from the file
